---
layout: base.njk
title: What the world is talking about
permalink: /dashboards/global-coverage/
three: true
description: "A live dashboard of what share of global news coverage mentions each big topic, day by day, built from GDELT Project data and refreshed every morning."
---
<div class="page-head">
  <div class="eyebrow">Dashboard · GDELT Project</div>
  <h1>What the world is talking about</h1>
  <p class="lede">GDELT monitors news websites in over 100 languages. This shows what share of English-language global coverage mentions each topic, day by day, going back up to a year.</p>
</div>

{# fixed colour per topic, so a topic missing for a day never repaints the others #}
{% set slots = { ai: 1, climate: 2, economy: 3, elections: 4 } %}
{% set chart = { label: 'Share of global news coverage by topic', unit: '%', series: [] } %}
{% for t in gdelt.topics %}{% set chart = (chart.series.push({ label: t.label, slot: slots[t.key], points: t.series }), chart) %}{% endfor %}

<div class="grid three">
  {% for t in insights.topics %}
  <div class="card stat">
    <div class="value">{{ t.last.toFixed(2) }}%</div>
    <div class="label"><b>{{ t.label }}</b> today · {% if t.change >= 0 %}up {{ t.change }}%{% else %}down {{ -t.change }}%{% endif %} on three months ago</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<section>
  <div class="card chart-card">
    <h2>Share of global news coverage</h2>
    <p class="muted">% of all monitored articles mentioning each topic, 7-day smoothed. Hover or tab into the chart for exact values.</p>
    <div class="ranges" data-range-for="coverage-chart" hidden role="group" aria-label="Time range">
      <button type="button" data-days="92">3M</button><button type="button" data-days="183">6M</button><button type="button" data-days="366">1Y</button>
    </div>
    <div class="chart" id="coverage-chart" data-chart="line" data-src="coverage-data"></div>
    <div class="legend">{% for t in gdelt.topics %}<span><i style="background:var(--series-{{ slots[t.key] }})"></i>{{ t.label }}</span>{% endfor %}</div>
    {% if insights.biggestPeak %}
    <p class="callout"><b>{{ insights.biggestPeak.label }}</b> had the biggest spike: {{ insights.biggestPeak.peak.value.toFixed(2) }}% of all global coverage on {{ insights.biggestPeak.peak.date | day }}.</p>
    {% endif %}
    <details class="table">
      <summary>View as table</summary>
      <div class="tablewrap"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Date</th>{% for t in gdelt.topics %}<th>{{ t.label }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for p in gdelt.topics[0].series | reverse %}{% set i = gdelt.topics[0].series.length - loop.index %}
          <tr><td>{{ p.date }}</td>{% for t in gdelt.topics %}<td>{{ t.series[i].value if t.series[i] else '' }}%</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </details>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">Source: <a href="https://www.gdeltproject.org/" rel="noopener">GDELT DOC 2.0 API</a>. Updated {{ gdelt.updated | when }}.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <div class="card chart-card">
    <h2>The coverage landscape, in 3D</h2>
    <p class="muted">Average weekly share of global coverage over {{ insights.grid.weeks.length }} weeks. Each row is a topic, each bar a week. Drag to rotate, hover a bar for its value.</p>
    <div class="grid3d" data-grid3d data-src="grid-data"></div>
    <div class="legend">{% for t in insights.grid.topics %}<span><i style="background:var(--series-{{ t.slot }});height:10px;width:10px;border-radius:2px"></i>{{ t.label }}</span>{% endfor %}</div>
  </div>
</section>
<script type="application/json" id="grid-data">{{ insights.grid | json | safe }}</script>
<script type="application/json" id="coverage-data">{{ chart | json | safe }}</script>
